@Xichen96 Reviewed head `68dc16a8eb2f37ec432657f4f190dcfa511a371c`. **Code LGTM for the bounded-retry scope; no new blocking findings.**

The rebase retains master's `finally` lock cleanup and lease-clear acknowledgement protocol. A failed read skips STATE_DB reconciliation and completion acknowledgement; the retry loop performs at most three read attempts with two 50 ms delays. Normal completed-file parsing and SmartSwitch lease-key behavior remain unchanged.

The remaining operational caveat is intentional: after retry exhaustion, the exception still propagates out of the signal callback and terminates `dhcpservd`. Recovery depends on configuration and restart limits, and may restart the whole container, interrupting Kea. This change does not provide atomic snapshots or reconstruct the full lease set across LFC files; those are pre-existing limitations outside this repair's scope.
